{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Come, eat of my bread</b> — the bet in בלחמי is in place of mem; likewise the bet in ביין מסכתי (in my mixed wine), as in: \"what remains of the flesh and of the bread.\" Their meaning is like: \"Ho, everyone who thirsts, come to the water,\" for everything is prepared for the meal."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:21:39.462804638Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}